  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: H. Konstantinos, on Imbros</p>\r\n<p>This place should not be confused with the <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../501511\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">Sanctuary of the Great Gods</a> on the nearby island of Samothrace.</p>\r\n<p>The sanctuary retaining wall was originally misidentified by Fredrich as part of a dam or other structure for collecting water for the ancient city of Imbros.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A sanctuary of the \"Great Gods\" on the Aegean island of Imbros/G\u00f6k\u00e7eada. The remains of the sanctuary are located southwest of modern Kalek\u00f6y, to the west of the airport in the vicinity of a ruined monastery of Agios Konstantinos at a place formerly known as Roxado.",
